---
// Recurring "plate number" running-head, echoing the numbered section
// pattern already used in PROJECT_BRIEF.md's proposed case-study layout
// (01 CONTEXT / 02 APPROACH / 03 SYSTEM). Sits at the top of each homepage
// section below the hero as a quiet, book-like index — content is generic
// (index + label props), so it belongs in ui/, not sections/.
//
// The optional "suffix" slot renders inline right after the label, for the
// rare section that needs a trailing mark next to its own heading (e.g.
// CurrentlyWorkingOn's terracotta wink asterisk) instead of a separate
// absolutely-positioned element guessing at the label's flow position.
//
// `index` is optional - CurrentlyWorkingOn dropped its own number when it
// moved to sit directly below Selected Work (per direct request), so the
// page's numbered running-head sequence (01 Selected Work, 02 Principles,
// 03 Gallery) stays a clean ascending read without a section physically
// sitting out of order in it. Omitting `index` just skips the "( NN )"
// line entirely rather than rendering an empty pair of parens.
//
// Layout pass ("subtitle Option 2," chosen from 3 live comparisons -
// see AGENTS.md for the other two): the index used to sit inline before
// the label on one baseline ("( 01 )  SELECTED WORK"). It's now a small
// kicker line stacked above the label instead, and a new optional
// `description` prop renders a paragraph - a short paragraph rather than
// running the full width underneath, so the eye travels down and across
// rather than in one straight vertical block. `description` is a plain
// prop (not a slot) deliberately: Astro slots aren't shadow DOM, so a
// paragraph passed in via `<slot>` would keep the *calling* component's
// own scope and SectionMarker's `<style>` block couldn't reach it
// without `:global()` (the same Astro-scoping trap documented elsewhere
// in this project, e.g. Button.astro's own comment on it) - a plain
// string prop keeps the paragraph inside SectionMarker's own template
// instead, so its styling lives in exactly one place and stays
// consistent everywhere this component is used.
//
// Scale-up pass, direct follow-up with a reference screenshot: "section
// titles can be a lot bigger... titles with 2 or more words... are
// broken up on different lines. the paragraph aligns more on the right
// of the page." Three changes, all in the label/description relationship
// - the kicker index above it is untouched, per direct instruction ("not
// the number or the paragraph"):
//
// 1. `.section-marker__label`'s font-size ceiling roughly doubled (2.75rem
//    -> ~6rem). The index/paragraph keep their previous sizes entirely.
// 2. The label now sits in a constrained-width grid column (roughly 7/12)
//    instead of running the section's full width - at this much bigger
//    size, a multi-word label like "Selected work" no longer fits that
//    column on one line and wraps at the natural word boundary ("SELECTED"
//    / "WORK"), which is what actually produces the two-line break the
//    reference shows. This is deliberately *not* a hardcoded line break
//    per label (e.g. a manual <br/> after the first word) - that would
//    only happen to work for two-word titles and silently do the wrong
//    thing for "Gallery" (one word, stays one line) or "My design
//    principles" (three words, wraps differently) the moment either
//    changes. A width-constrained column wraps correctly for whatever
//    label text shows up, forever, with no per-label special-casing.
// 3. `.section-marker__description` moved out of the flow entirely,
//    into its own grid column pushed to the section's right edge -
//    "aligns more on the right of the page," not just indented a fixed
//    distance from the label the way the previous pass did it.
interface Props {
  index?: string;
  label: string;
  description?: string;
}

const { index, label, description } = Astro.props;
---

<div class="section-marker">
  {index && (
    <p class="section-marker__index" aria-hidden="true">
      ( {index} )
    </p>
  )}
  <h2 class="section-marker__label">
    {label}
    <slot name="suffix" />
  </h2>
  {description && <p class="section-marker__description">{description}</p>}
</div>

<style>
  .section-marker {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(12, 1fr);
    column-gap: var(--space-32);
    align-items: end;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .section-marker__index {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-label);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wide);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  /* Constrained well below the 7/12 grid column it sits in (below) -
     this is what actually makes a multi-word label wrap onto more than
     one line at the bigger size. Barlow Condensed is, true to its name,
     narrow per character: "SELECTED WORK" at 96px measures only ~554px
     unconstrained (confirmed directly, not assumed), well inside the
     7/12 column's own ~640px width at this content-max-width, so the
     column alone never triggered a wrap - a `max-width` in `ch`
     (font-size-relative, so it scales with the clamp() below rather
     than needing its own breakpoint ladder) is the thing actually doing
     the work. Tuned to wrap "Selected work" after the first word
     without leaving so little room that "Gallery" (the shortest real
     label) looks awkwardly starved for space. */
  .section-marker__label {
    grid-column: 1 / 8;
    max-width: 10ch;
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 6vw + 1rem, 6rem);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    line-height: 0.92;
  }

  /* Pushed into its own column at the section's right edge - "aligns
     more on the right of the page" - rather than indented a fixed
     distance from the label. align-items: end on the parent grid lines
     its own bottom edge up with the label's, echoing roughly where the
     reference screenshot sits it relative to the title block. */
  .section-marker__description {
    grid-column: 9 / 13;
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    /* The two-column split needs real width to read as "pushed to the
               right" rather than just cramped - below this, label and
               description both drop to a plain single stacked column, same
               "macro asymmetry drops at a width threshold" pattern used
               everywhere else in this project. */
    .section-marker {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      row-gap: 1.25rem;
    }

    .section-marker__label,
    .section-marker__description {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .section-marker__label {
      font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 10vw, 3.5rem);
    }
  }
</style>
